out: value: str:"lastIndex=0;index=0;length=2;0=2:kx;1=1:x;groups=1;<b>=1:x;indices=u"
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: str:"lastIndex=0;index=0;length=2;0=2:kx;1=1:x;groups=1;<b>=1:x;indices=u"
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: str:"lastIndex=0;index=0;length=2;0=2:kx;1=1:x;groups=1;<b>=1:x;indices=u"
divergence.broiler-js: row S5 as revised 2026-11-01 (owner's decision D-s5): \k in a class beside a named group without u or v, [\k<a>](?<a>x) and [\k](?<a>x), by the constructor, a literal never evaluated and an exec; Broiler.JS answers refused, a SyntaxError "invalid named reference": RegExpGroupNames refuses a \k inside a class whenever the pattern holds a group name, where B.1.2's ClassEscape reads ~NamedCaptureGroups and admits k as an identity escape, the outcome this vector's per-engine field holds (regexpref's reading, which revision 31 took); a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0081, by D-s5); answered by SJL-11.5, which deletes RegExpGroupNames' regular-expression prechecks (decision D20)
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regexpbuiltinexec spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-compilepattern spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-compilesubpattern spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-compilecharacterclass spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-compiletocharset spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-regular-expressions-patterns ref:regexpref@1
