divergence.broiler-js: row M3: line terminators without u: ^ and $ under m on U+2028 and U+2029 (exec, %Symbol.match% and %Symbol.split%), and $ without m before a final LF; Broiler.JS answers .NET's: under m only \r is added to .NET's \n (BuiltIns/RegExp/JSRegExp.cs:931-983 at 1f91b8f1), and $ without m matches before a final LF; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0081); answered by SJL-11.5, Broiler.JS's cut-over to Broiler.Regex
