id: regexp/matching/m7-backreference-surrogates/0011
area: regexp
op: RegExpBuiltinExec
in: str:"foo(.+)bar\\1" str:"v" str:"foo\uD834bar\uD834\uDC00" int:0
out: value: str:"lastIndex=0;null"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-vm: row M7: a back-reference under u or v across a surrogate pair, foo(.+)bar\1, \k<x>, (\ud834)\1 and the look-behind (?<=\1(.))b; Broiler.VM answers a match of half the pair: the back-reference compares code units (F/JsRegExpMatcher.cs:4642 at aaa39fb) with no check that it ends on a code point, and backwards starts the capture's length in code units before the position; a correction of Broiler.VM (kind R, JSD-0081); answered by SJL-11.4, Broiler.VM's cut-over to Broiler.Regex
